<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates higher on C. Bank rate hike.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates higher on C. Bank rate hike.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) rose in line with a two percentage-point rate hike in the Central Bank's overnight borrowing rate to 32 percent, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>However, &quot;the market was relatively quiet compared with the past days. The market is in stage of a consolidation,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>Banks are weighing the situation after the recent volatility in interest rates caused by speculation on the peso, he said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  JULY 10		JULY 9</p>
<p>    1 W		30  7/8		 29  5/8</p>
<p>    2 W		29  9/16		28  1/16</p>
<p>    1 M		27  5/8		 24 13/16</p>
<p>    2 M		23  1/4		 19  3/4</p>
<p>    3 M		20  5/16		18  1/16</p>
<p>    6 M		17 11/16		16  5/8</p>
<p>    12M		16 13/16		16</p>
<p>    VAL		11-Jul		  10-Jul</p>
<p>-- Lilian Karunungan (63 2) 841-8937</p>
